notes.body:
added option to statistics->TCP Stream graph->Duplication table. I had concerns about about adding a "table" to a section called "graph", but I didn't come up with a better place to put it. Any input would be appreciated. 
![image](/uploads/ee66da5cb9b62483e953bce32553fa28/image.png){width=900 height=530}

The table was somewhat modeled off the tcp stream graph, whereas the option to change streams is the same functionality, and clicking through the packets is the same.
![image](/uploads/a86729f17731634d701c588aeb6f23fe/image.png){width=900 height=370}

I added three options. Two were necessary one: to turn the option on/off. two: define the time to look for true duplicates. The third option I added because I didn't like the default way how a detected duplicate did not have the tcp analysis flags from the original/first packet, so I thought I should have a way for the user to allow the current behavior vs the way I was wanting it to carry the tcp analysis flags from the original packet.
![image](/uploads/920aa2ca3b725c18c751a5e9de0a9961/image.png){width=846 height=222}

I purposely referred to everything the options and display as "duplication" as to not be confused with the current "duplicate" tcp analysis that exist. Though it is close, I couldn't come up with a better name for it. So if there is any concerns, or input on alternatives please let me know.

